  ['Can gut problems cause acne?', 'They may play a role for some people, mainly through inflammation, but acne also depends on hormones, oil production, genetics and skincare. If your acne is persistent or painful, a dermatologist can look at the whole picture.'],
  ['What are the signs of a damaged skin barrier?', 'Tightness, dehydration, redness, burning or stinging, flaking and sudden sensitivity to products that used to feel fine. They point to a barrier that is struggling and have many possible causes, not only the gut.'],
